# Metaviews Trust

Canonical site: {{ site.url }}

Metaviews Trust is a commercial microsite for Metaviews Media Management Ltd. It explains founder-led AI trust, stakeholder buy-in, open-source AI literacy, and adoption-capacity work for Canadian organizations responding to the current AI adoption moment.

Primary page:
- {{ site.url }} — AI Trust, Buy-In, and Adoption Capacity

Core positioning:
- Metaviews helps Canadian organizations turn AI pressure into practical curiosity, shared literacy, stakeholder buy-in, and trustworthy adoption.
- The work is led by Jesse Hirsh and grows out of his long-running public practice translating internet, media, algorithmic, and institutional change into usable language for decision-makers and communities.
- The site emphasizes buy-in before rollout: adoption work should involve workers, managers, executives, boards, customers, members, partners, funders, regulators, or other stakeholders early enough to shape successful projects.
- Open source is presented as a literacy, trust, and sovereignty strategy, not as a generic technical preference.

Jesse Hirsh / founder context:
- Jesse Hirsh leads Metaviews and shapes this AI trust briefing work directly.
- His work connects AI adoption and governance, media literacy, disinformation, institutional trust, technology and authority, public communication, and practical organizational judgment.
- Reference pages: https://jessehirsh.com/ ; https://www.nsb.com/speakers/jesse-hirsh/ ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jesse_Hirsh

